spans.s:
--seven in number, one above the other like several umbrellas spread over. To the usual seven are added वैकुण्ठ and Golokam;
1: Br. II. १९. १५५-6; २१. १९. २१; III. ४१. ५४-5.
the fourteen sthalas or places of which seven are कृत and seven are अकृत; भूः and other six are कृतस्; the अकृतस् are प्राकृतस्; पृथ्वी, अन्तरिक्ष, दिव्य and महर्लोकस् are known as अर्णवकस् or which stand until आभूतसम्प्लव; जन, तप and सब्य are ज्ञानलोकस्; व्यक्तलोकस् are भूः, भुवः, स्वः, मह, जन, तप and सत्य (Brahma); their residents are given, those attaining Brahmaloka (सत्य) do not have rebirth.
2: वा. १०१. १०-39; Vi. I. २२. ८०;

--eight in number, each with a city of his own situated in the eight cardinal points, surrounding the outskirts of ब्रह्मा's city;
1: भा. V. १६. २९.
stand in the midst of लोकालोक, on the four sides of Meru in their respective towns: East- India in वस्वौकसार: South-Yama in Samyamana: West- वरुण in Sukha and North-Candra in विभावरि. These are stationed round the मानस lake for the protection of Dharma and progress of the world;
2: Br. II. २१. २८-34, १५६;

. १०२; M. १२४. ९४; वा. ५०. ८६, ९१; १११. २५.
an अम्श of the Supreme Lord;
3: M. ५२. २१.
served तारक as servants; beaten by तारक;
4: Ib. १४८. २७; १५३. १८३.
served in the battle of Tripura;
5: Ib. २४. 5; १३८. 1.
requested Soma to restore तारा back to बृहस्पति;
6: Ib. २३. ३५.
oblations to, in rituals of digging tanks and planting gardens;
7: Ib. ५८. ३३; ५९. १०.
invoked in making the १६ gifts;
